## Copy this file to .env (dev) and set the same keys in your host's env vars
## (e.g. Vercel Project Settings -> Environment Variables) for production.
##
## Get these from your Supabase project: Project Settings -> API.
## Accounts (sign up / login / saved trips) are disabled until both are set.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

## Travelpayouts partner ID (Dashboard -> your Aviasales program -> marker).
## Tags the outbound "check this fare" link so the click is attributed to you.
## Public by design (it rides in the link's query string), but kept out of the
## repo so dev/preview/production can be told apart. Unset = unmarked
## Skyscanner links, which is the correct default for a fork or a local build.
VITE_TP_MARKER=

## Omio affiliate tracking link (Impact network). In the Impact dashboard:
## Brands -> Omio -> Create link, then paste the generated link here, e.g.
## https://omio.sjv.io/c/1234567/898765/12345 . Tags the "Omio" booking link
## on train/bus legs so the click-out is attributed to you (src/lib/omio.js
## appends u=<route page> and subId1=<surface> per click). Public by design,
## kept out of the repo for the same reasons as VITE_TP_MARKER. Unset = legs
## show only the operator and Google Maps links, no Omio entry.
VITE_OMIO_TRACKING_LINK=

## AI day planner: there is deliberately NO client-side key for it. The Gemini
## key lives ONLY as a Supabase Edge Function secret (never VITE_-prefixed;
## anything VITE_ is compiled into the public bundle):
##   supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=...
## Setup + zero-billing rules: supabase/functions/plan-day/README.md
